  /* TRAINED BY THE EMPLOYER. The aviation authority, the pipeline company,
   * KenGen, the ports authority, the railway, the roads department and the
   * revenue authority all run their own institutes, and a learner reading Njia
   * would never have known. Two things stand out and are worth reading off the
   * records rather than the prose:
   *
   * Aviation is the most expensive route in this catalogue by a wide margin —
   * the avionics diploma at Wilson Airport is a published Ksh 446,000 — and the
   * fee, not the grade, is what actually excludes people from it.
   *
   * Several of these institutes publish no fee at all. Those records carry null
   * and say so. A learner who knows a figure is missing can ring and ask; one
   * given a confident guess cannot tell there is anything to check. */
